# Architecture Rules - Feature Sliced Design (FSD)

## Layer Structure

```
src/
├── app/                  # FSD App layer (providers, global styles)
├── pages/                # FSD Pages layer (page components)
├── widgets/              # FSD Widgets layer (complex UI blocks)
├── features/             # FSD Features layer (business functions)
├── entities/             # FSD Entities layer (business entities)
└── shared/               # FSD Shared layer (common resources)
```

## Layer Dependencies

- `shared` → `entities` → `features` → `widgets` → `pages` → `app`
- Layers can only import from lower layers
- No circular dependencies allowed

## Next.js App Router Structure

```
app/                      # Next.js App Router (root)
├── layout.tsx           # Root layout
├── page.tsx             # Home page
├── events/page.tsx      # Imports from src/pages/events
├── tasks/page.tsx       # Imports from src/pages/tasks
├── calendar/page.tsx    # Imports from src/pages/calendar
└── journal/page.tsx     # Imports from src/pages/journal
```

## Entity Structure

Each entity should have:

```
entities/entity-name/
├── api/
│   ├── entity-name.api.ts
│   └── entity-name.routes.ts
├── model/
│   ├── entity-name.types.ts
│   ├── entity-name.schemas.ts
│   └── entity-name.queries.ts
├── ui/
│   ├── entity-name-card.tsx
│   └── entity-name-card.module.css
└── index.ts
```

## Public API

- Each layer should have `index.ts` files
- Only export what's necessary for other layers
- Don`t use barrel exports

## Import Order

1. React and Next.js imports
2. Third-party libraries
3. Shared layer imports
4. Entity layer imports
5. Feature layer imports
6. Widget layer imports
7. Page layer imports
8. App layer imports
